content.text:
Great. Now write app.js. This is where the real work is.

Let me plan code in detail and write it in chunks. Given its size, perhaps 1000+ lines. I'll write carefully.

Start with constants, utilities, dom references, config, state.

```js
(() => {
  'use strict';
  const Core = window.VitariumCore;
  if (!Core) return;
  const { Ecosystem, CATS } = Core;

  const $ = (sel, root=document) => root.querySelector(sel);
  const $$ = ...;
  const clamp = ...
  const pad = ...
  const fmt = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US');
  const MONO = getComputedStyle(document.body).getPropertyValue('--mono');
  // computed CSS vars return the font stack with quotes; canvas font can use that? Use fixed string.
```

Canvas font:
`'10px "SF Mono", "JetBrains Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace'`. Use `FONT_MONO = '10px "SF Mono", "JetBrains Mono", Menlo, monospace'`.
Serif not used in canvas much (chart titles DOM). Use mono for axes.

Colors:
```
const rootStyle = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
const hex = (v)=>rootStyle.getPropertyValue(v).trim();
const C = {...};
function rgba(hexColor, a) { ... }
```
Need to handle hex strings; all plain. For rules, use `hex` with alpha. If a value is like `#...`, fine.
`C.rule = rootStyle.getPropertyValue('--rule').trim()` returns rgba; can use directly.
`C.bg = ...`.
- For alpha colors from hex.

Species:
```
const SPECIES = [
 { key:'plant', name:'Virens', binom:'Virens', role:'rosette', className:'sp-plant', glyph:'g-virens', varName:'--plant', genes:[...] },
 ...
]
```
Engine history traits keys are 'plant','prey','pred'.

Event meta:
```
const EVENTS = {
 drought: { label:'Drought', kicker:'Disturbance I', note:'The canopy withholds. Growth is arrested.', duration: 18, color:()=>C.drought },
 ...
}
```
Use color variables directly. For the UI event color, set inline CSS custom property.

Config and state.

DOM cache:
```
const els = {
 metaSeed: $('metaSeed'), ...
}
```
Maybe lazy `$` in functions for simplicity. But repeated queries each frame could hurt. Cache in an object at init.

Trait DOM build.

Utility `setText(el, value)` if changed to reduce writes.
`formatInt(n)` use toLocaleString? Use `String(n)` with pad for counts. `pad(n,4)` for counts; but 4000+ is 4 digits, comma? Use `n.toLocaleString('en-US').padStart(4,'0')` would stripear; e.g., '4,297' length 5. Fine. For counts under 1000 like 229, show '0229'. For consistency use 4-digit zero-padded without commas (up to 9999). Plants max 5188; prey 700; pred 100. Great: `String(n).padStart(4,'0')`.
For archive counts use comma-separated: `n.toLocaleString('en-US')`.

Event interval padded 3: `pad(v,3)`.

Seed padded 6: `pad(seed,6)`.

Formatting numbers in chart:
- use fmt.

Floating format:
```
const f2 = (v) => v.toFixed(2);
const f3 = (v) => v.toFixed(3);
const fSigned = (v, digits=2) => (v>=0?'+':'−') + Math.abs(v).toFixed(digits);
```
Use minus sign `\u2212` for typography; could use '-' for compatibility. Use Unicode minus. The file already has Unicode.

State:
```
const state = {
 engine:null, running:true, complete:false, fastForwarding:false,
 acc:0, lastTime:performance.now(), lastGen:-1, lastUiLog:-1, headlessSeen:...,
 drawerOpen:true, archiveOpen:false, archiveRevealPending:false,
 lastPaused:false, lastKillSeen:0, seenLogs:0, dispatchTimer:0, ledgerTimer:0,
 hoverChartX:null, chartHover:null,
 dirty:true, lastMetaState:''
};
```

Initialization:
```
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init); // script at end; can call init directly
```
Script at end of body, so elements exist; call `init()`.

Init:
- cache? done.
- buildTraitTable.
- bind controls.
- drawStatic dial/sparks? After layout. 
- `startRun({initial:true})`.
- register resize.
- rAF.

Create engine:
```
function engineParams(){
 const e = {};
 ...
}
function newEngine(){
 const params = {...}
 state.engine = new Ecosystem(params);
 state.seenLogs = 0; // process initial seal? We don't want dispatch. We'll set ledger separately.
 updateAll(true);
}
```
- The engine options include `width`, `height`? The renderer knows 120×80. Core defaults; no need.
- `initPrey` etc. default.

On start:
```
function startRun({seed = config.seed, keep?}){
  state.engine = new Ecosystem({...});
  state.complete=false; state.fastForwarding=false; state.running=true; state.acc=0;
  state.lastGen=-1; state.lastUiLog=0; state.ledgerIndex=-1;
  state.acc...;
  state.engine.seen... 
  // initial ledger from engine.logs[0]
  setLedger(engine.logs[0]);
  state.seenLogs = engine.logs.length; // avoid announcing seal
  closeArchive instant if open;
  updateAll();
  drawAllSparks();
  setStateUI();
  renderer.dirty = true;
  hideDispatch();
  requestAnimationFrame(() => { ... });
}
```
Wait seenLogs should start at 0 and process the seal? We can set `seenLogs = 1` after using the seal. The seal has kind 'seal'. Fine. The ledger initial is the seal. At events/migrations, process new logs.
- On restart, the field automatically runs (running=true).
- If archive was open, remove open/hidden; set shell inert false. Need closeArchive.

`setStateUI()`:
```
const status = state.fastForwarding ? 'HEADLESS' : state.complete ? 'CLOSED' : state.running ? 'OBSERVING' : 'SUSPENDED';
metaState.textContent=status; liveDot class...
pauseBtn aria-pressed = !running; label = running ? 'Suspend' : 'Resume'; icon use href...
pauseBtn disabled = state.complete or fastForwarding;
headlessBtn disabled = state.complete or fastForwarding;
```
- If paused because fast-forward, pauseBtn disabled. 
- The stage strike still.
- The meta state text maybe "OBSERVING" all caps.
- Use `pauseLabel.textContent`.
- Set `aria-label`? The button text is enough. `data-tip`.
- Update `document.title`? Could show generation; no.

Live updates:
```
function updateCounts() {
 if (state.engine.gen !== state.lastGen || state.forceUi) {
  const {plants,prey,preds}=...
  setText(countPlant,pad(plants.length,4))...
  setText(metaGen, pad(gen,4));
  setText(metaSpan, pad(config.runLength,4));
  updateActiveChips(); updateEventReadouts(); updateNext(); updateEta();
  processLogs(); // But logs might need processing even if gen same? events happen on step. Call in afterStep.
  state.lastGen=gen;
 }
}
```
- Every step, call `afterStep()`:
  - process new logs.
  - update counts, active chips, event readouts, next, eta.
  - renderer dirty? always while running.
- On param changes, update just relevant UI.
- Avoid full DOM churn every gen? It's 12/s; fine. Rebuild chips only if active set/remaining changed. Use cached text.
- `updateActiveChips`: active Map; build HTML string with fixed labels; use `innerHTML` safe (labels fixed). Need color var inline `style="--ev: var(--drought)"`. Add chips. If none, show weather element; keep the weather node, toggle hidden. If rebuilding, using innerHTML loses the weather element. Better:
  - On init, clear head events and append a persistent `<span class=weather id=weather>`? It's already there. We can hide it and remove previously generated chips. Use a separate container for chips appended after the weather. In HTML `headEvents` contains weather; JS can `headEvents.querySelectorAll('.chip')` remove and then hide weather. Simpler: set `headEvents.innerHTML` each update with either weather or chips. Recreating a tiny span 12/s is okay. But `aria-live` will may announce changes each time. The headEvents has `aria-live=polite`; rebuilding could be noisy. Replace with `aria-live=off` and add a separate announcer? The active chips change every gen; don't want screen reader spam. Remove `aria-live` from headEvents or keep but don't rebuild if unchanged. Build a key from active types + remaining values; remaining changes every gen, so would rebuild every gen. Better show the remaining as a separate text node and update it, but that still could announce. Let's remove aria-live from the headEvents and rely on the dispatch banner (role status) and the announcer. The user can navigate to the chips. Use static `aria-label` updated maybe. 
  - In markup, headEvents has aria-live="polite"; I'll change to aria-label="Active disturbances" without aria-live. The `.dispatch` role=status announces. Also the sr announcer. 
  - Update chips only when the type set changes; update remaining text nodes each gen. Use a helper that compares the active key. Show/hide weather. To build chips, create elements. Include the event's label + `<span class=left>12G</span>`. The chip title. Use event colors.
  - The active remaining changes each gen; update text content. That's fine visually. 
  - To avoid aria-live spam, no live region.
- Process logs:
```
function processLogs(announce=true){
 const logs = engine.logs;
 if (seenLogs >= logs.length) return;
 let latest=null, latestStart=null;
 for (i=seenLogs;i<logs.length;i++){
   const l=logs[i];
   latest=l;
   if (l.kind==='start' && announce) latestStart=l;
   if (l.kind==='start') announceScreenReader(`Generation ${l.gen}. ${l.title}. ${l.detail}`);
   if (l.kind==='migration' || l.kind==='extinct') announceScreenReader(...);
 }
 seenLogs=logs.length;
 if (latestStart) showDispatch(latestStart);
 if (latest) setLedger(latest);
}
```
  - If fast-forwarding, announce=false and only update ledger at the end. 
- `setLedger(log)`: fade text. Use:
```
const html = `<span class="ledger-gen">${pad(log.gen,4)}</span><span class="ledger-title">${title}</span><span class="ledger-detail"> — ${detail}</span>`;
```
Use textContent for title? Titles/details are from our fixed logs; safe. Build a DOM fragment to be clean. We can set innerHTML; logs are internal fixed strings, no user input. Fine.
  - Fade via class; if called often, clear timer. 
- Next event:
```
const types = Object.keys(EVENTS);
let best=null;
for type: if enabled && interval>0 && nextAt finite: if nextAt < best.at ...;
if no best -> "NONE BEFORE CLOSE"/"QUIET". If best.at > runLength -> "BEYOND THE SPAN" or "NONE WITHIN SPAN". If event active, still show next; maybe label with the active event? We'll choose next future.
```
  - InnerHTML `<span class="dot" style="background:..."></span>${name} @ ${pad(gen,4)}`; currently CSS dot uses currentColor; set style color on wrapper. Use `nextEvent.style.color = C[type]`? The whole text would be event-colored. The `.next-value` default muted. Maybe set the dot only. Build with a span style background. 
  - If the next event is within e.g. 5 gens, add "IN 5". Keep.
  - If all disabled, "NONE SCHEDULED".
- Event row readouts:
  - Each `.event` data-enabled; set.
  - The interval display padded? The `.event-value` shows `<span id=droughtValue>110</span>` — set "0110"? The initial template shows 110. The readout unit. Use 3-digit padded for instrument consistency: set "110" or "0110"? The slider note says gen. Use "110" to avoid leading zero confusion. In the "next @ 0110" pad. Keep event value as integer text.
  - If disabled, value `.is-off` and maybe text "OFF" while the interval remains available? Could show `<span id=droughtValue>OFF</span>` losing the interval. Better show the interval with the `.event-value` dim and set the next label "disabled". The toggle indicates. Good.
  - `next-at`:
    - active: `ACTIVE · ${remaining}G LEFT`
    - enabled: if gen >= runLength -> "span closed"; else if nextAt > runLength -> "beyond span"; else `next @ ${pad(nextAt,4)}`
    - disabled: "disabled"
  - This updates each gen. Set textContent only if changed.
- ETA:
  - remaining = max(0, config.runLength - gen); seconds = remaining / tempo; format. `tempoEta.innerHTML = `${dur} <em>at ${tempo.toFixed(1)}×</em>``. This updates each gen; 12/s innerHTML; use two spans to avoid churn? Simpler set innerHTML at gen rate; fine. Could update every 0.5s. We'll only update when the whole-second changes. Use a cache.
- Next event and eta update each gen. Fine.

- Counts update in the head and meta; update if changed to avoid DOM churn.

Controls binding:
- Generic `createSlider(opts)`. Attach to elements by id. Ensure CSS fill initial.
- Use pointer capture; `pointermove` on element. On pointerdown set focus and immediately update. Also support `wheel`? Not necessary; could be nice but hijacks page scroll. Skip.
- Add double-click to reset default? Nice for power users, but not required. Could implement dblclick resets to default. Tooltip mention? Skip.
- For sliders, the sparkline is drawn on input. 
- The slider's `aria-valuetext` callback.
- The event slider `data-tip` not set; add tooltips by setting data-tip attributes in JS based on type? Add to the slider element `data-tip = type`. Fine. The event row/switch already. We'll attach tooltips to elements with data-tip, including dynamically added ones. Initialize tooltips by delegated listeners on document, not per element. That handles all. Great:
  - On pointerover/pointerout/focusin/focusout of `[data-tip]`, show/hide.
  - For focus, use focusin on document; check closest.
  - For hover, pointerover; pointerout. Avoid flicker moving within children: use relatedTarget and contains. The element is the slider itself.
  - TIPS map keys. The event sliders can get data-tip from type. Mutation etc.
- Tooltip positioning:
```
function showTip(el){
 const key=el.dataset.tip; const t=TIPS[key]; if(!t) return;
 tip.innerHTML = `<span class=tip-title>${t.title}</span><span class=tip-body>${t.body}</span>`;
 tip.classList.add('show'); tip.setAttribute('aria-hidden','false');
 const rect = el.getBoundingClientRect();
 requestAnimationFrame(() => {
   const tw = tip.offsetWidth, th=tip.offsetHeight;
   let left = rect.left + rect.width/2 - tw/2;
   left = clamp(left, 8, innerWidth - tw - 8);
   let top = rect.top - th - 10;
   if (top < 8) top = rect.bottom + 10;
   top = clamp(top, 8, innerHeight - th - 8);
   tip.style.left = `${Math.round(left)}px`;
   tip.style.top = `${Math.round(top)}px`;
 });
}
```
- `tip` initially `hidden` attribute? In markup it's a div with hidden? No, it has `.tip`. Add `aria-hidden=true`. CSS opacity 0; pointer-events none. Fine. Keep in DOM. When showing, set content. 
- Hide on `pointerleave`, `focusout`, Escape, scroll, pointerdown elsewhere? Add.
- Hovering the panel etc. Fine.
- Tooltip for pause changes with state? TIPS static; the button label updates. Fine.

- The seed sparkline fingerprint should update immediately when the input value changes (on commit). 
- New seed button: `deriveSeed(config.seed)`; sets seed & restarts. Replay button restart same seed with same current settings? As discussed. We'll implement replay current settings.
- On seed change, if the same, maybe just restart? A restart is expected.

- run length stepper:
  - The readout is not an input; add keyboard to it? Make it role=spinbutton tabindex 0 in markup? Could modify it with JS. Add attributes:
```
spanRead.tabIndex = 0; role spinbutton; aria-valuemin...; aria-valuenow...
```
  - On ArrowUp/Down: change 50; PageUp/Down 250. Enter? no. The +/- buttons already.
  - Call `setRunLength`.
- `setRunLength(v)`:
```
v = clamp(roundTo50, 100, 2000);
