The last media query duplicate is redundant (body already hidden when archive-open). Fine.

Now the build script. It should inline sim.js and app.js into index.html, and maybe check for external URLs. Write `_dev/build.js`:
```
const fs=require('fs');
const t=fs.readFileSync('_dev/template.html','utf8');
const sim=fs.readFileSync('_dev/sim.js','utf8');
const app=fs.readFileSync('_dev/app.js','utf8');
const out=t.replace('/*__SIM__*/', ()=>sim).replace('/*__APP__*/', ()=>app);
fs.writeFileSync('index.html',out);
```
Need avoid `$&` interpretation by replace; use functions. Also ensure no `</script>` occurs in sim/app (the sim code has no; app has none). Add a check.
- Place the final index.html at workspace root.
- Maybe remove the `'use strict'` duplicated? Each script; fine.
- The sim IIFE root uses `typeof globalThis !== 'undefined' ? globalThis : this`; fine. It will attach VitariumCore globally. The `module` guard false in browser (module undefined). Fine.
- `/*__SIM__*/` appears once; `/*__APP__*/` once. Good.
- Build outputs. Then open in Chrome via CDP.

Let's write build and a CDP harness.

